        "title": "Clarify AIG service-backed scanner setup",
        "body": "Refs #5.\n\nDocuments the AIG scanner as a service-backed integration, surfaces setup and smoke-test hints in scanner metadata, publishes the A.I.G guide in the generated docs site, and clarifies why it is not installed by the local scanner installer.\n\nBehavior proof:\n```text\n$ make docs-site\nBuilt 7 docs page(s) in dist/docs-site\n\n$ ls dist/docs-site | grep aig.html\naig.html\n\n$ clawscan scanners aig\nService-backed: yes\nSmoke test: AIG_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8088 clawscan ./README.md --scanner aig --sandbox off --json\nInstall: Run the A.I.G Docker/API service separately on localhost or a private network; ClawScan does not start or expose it. See docs/aig.md for the service setup and smoke recipe.\n\n$ clawscan install aig\nScanner aig has no local scanner CLI to install. Run the A.I.G Docker/API service separately on localhost or a private network; ClawScan does not start or expose it. See docs/aig.md for the service setup and smoke recipe.\n```",
